---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Host a 24/7 airport camera | Airport Runways Live"
  description="Pitch for rooftop, hotel, and warehouse hosts who want a 24/7 runway camera via Axis PTZ, CamStreamer, and Flightradar24."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">V4</p>
      <h1>Host a cam</h1>
      <p>
        Got a rooftop, hotel, or warehouse with a runway view? The industry path for a real 24/7 airport camera is an
        Axis PTZ, CamStreamer’s PlaneTracker app, and a Flightradar24 partnership for ADS-B overlay and YouTube
        distribution.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not claim a 24/7 MCO camera that does not exist. If no roof ever happens, the company is still complete.
        The cam is an upgrade: a tile on the board and a 24/7 YouTube (or FR24 partner) stream. It is not a substitute
        for talking on mic.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Clear, legal sightline to a runway or final</li>
        <li>Power, network, and a place the camera can live for years</li>
        <li>Property-owner permission. No drones in Class B without authorization.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        CamStreamer’s host program:{' '}
        <a href="https://camstreamer.com/planetracker-about" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          camstreamer.com/planetracker-about
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <form class="form" data-mailto-form data-subject="Host a cam">
        <div class="form-grid">
          <div>
            <label for="name">Name</label>
            <input id="name" name="name" required />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="email">Email</label>
            <input id="email" name="email" type="email" required />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="place">Property / city / airport</label>
          <input id="place" name="place" required />
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="message">What can you see?</label>
          <textarea id="message" name="message" required></textarea>
        </div>
        <button class="btn btn-amber" type="submit">Email {site.email}</button>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  import { bindMailtoForm } from '../scripts/mailto-form.ts';
  bindMailtoForm();
</script>
